  "summary": "Malicious code in evm-validation (npm)",
  "details": "The package exports a `validated` function that, when called, sends its string argument to a remote endpoint at hxxps://e-api[.]netlify[.]app/ via an HTTP GET. The endpoint URL is obfuscated in the source (ROT13 cipher plus string reversal) to hide it. The package is presented as an EVM validation utility, but its only real behaviour is forwarding caller-supplied data to this remote host — a data-exfiltration beacon.",
